  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader on the iPhone Duo in landscape, I want one refresh control at the end of the topic, so that the page is not cluttered by a duplicate. Operator feedback, 2026-11-27 (screenshot kept off the tracker: it shows real members' posts).\n\n### Observed (operator's iPhone Duo, landscape, dark, topic reader at the last page)\n- The **end-of-page** refresh control under the last message (spinner while reloading): **keep**, it is right.\n- A **second circular refresh button floats over the last message**, in the middle of its body, next to an embedded image: **too much**, to remove.\n- « peut-être d'autres » : check the other sizes and orientations (iPhone portrait, iPad, Duo folded).\n\n### To check first\nIdentify what the floating control is before removing it: a second instance of the reader's refresh overlay (e.g. the pull-to-refresh / « load more » affordance positioned against the wrong frame in landscape), or the per-image retry badge of a failed or pending image. If it is the image retry badge, it must not look like the page refresh (separate issue if so).\n\n### Acceptance\n- One page-refresh control in the reader at the end of the last page, in every size class and orientation; a hosted or snapshot test pins it for the Duo landscape size.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
